"whatsNew.110.inApp.title" = "XSide module in the apps";
"whatsNew.110.inApp.text" = "Every app XSide installs now has its own XSide settings, per device, kept in step between your Mac and your iPhone. Change a setting on either side: the most recent change wins.";
"whatsNew.110.page.title" = "XSide Settings on the iPhone";
"whatsNew.110.page.text" = "Settings > Apps > [app name] > XSide Settings, or faster: touch and hold the app's icon > XSide Settings. A page of its own, translated by iOS, with the validity date, the last refresh, the version and the switches.";
"whatsNew.110.pill.title" = "Validity when opening";
"whatsNew.110.pill.text" = "On each launch, a bar at the top says how many days the app stays valid, then goes away. On by default; you can turn it off per app.";
"whatsNew.110.late.title" = "An alert when it's late";
"whatsNew.110.late.text" = "If XSide couldn't refresh the app in time, the bar turns orange, then red under a day, and says what to do. An app with automatic refresh turned off says so instead.";
"whatsNew.110.card.title" = "The card after a refresh, optional";
"whatsNew.110.card.text" = "The card at the bottom after a refresh or an update can now be turned off, app by app.";
"whatsNew.110.reminder.title" = "The reminder, per app";
"whatsNew.110.reminder.text" = "The reminder before expiry is now set per app, on the iPhone or on the Mac, instead of one switch for all.";
"whatsNew.110.language.title" = "XSide messages language";
"whatsNew.110.language.text" = "Choose the language of XSide's messages in each app: automatic (the iPhone's), English or French.";
"whatsNew.110.level.title" = "All, Essentials or None";
"whatsNew.110.level.text" = "On the Mac, one choice sets how much XSide shows in an app: everything, only the alerts, or nothing (not even the first-install window).";
"whatsNew.110.quick.title" = "Touch and hold the icon";
"whatsNew.110.quick.text" = "Touch and hold an app's icon: XSide Settings, Refresh now, Report a problem, right from the install. They come after the app's own quick actions written in the app (iOS shows 4).";
"whatsNew.110.phone.title" = "Refresh from the iPhone";
"whatsNew.110.phone.text" = "Ask XSide to refresh an app from the app itself, over your local network. The channel is signed and private to each app: nobody else on the network can use it.";
"whatsNew.110.pause.title" = "Pause from the iPhone";
"whatsNew.110.pause.text" = "Turn off \"Automatic refresh\" in an app's iOS Settings to stop refreshing it. The panel says it was paused from the iPhone, the iPad or the Mac.";
"whatsNew.110.network.title" = "Patient with the Mac";
"whatsNew.110.network.text" = "The first time, iOS asks to allow the local network, and macOS may ask to allow incoming connections for XSide (explained in the app). The iPhone waits and retries up to 20 seconds instead of giving up.";
"whatsNew.110.onLaunch.title" = "Refresh at next opening";
"whatsNew.110.onLaunch.text" = "In an app's iOS Settings, \"Refresh at next launch\" asks XSide for a refresh the next time you open the app, without opening it first.";
"whatsNew.110.steps.title" = "An install window in three steps";
"whatsNew.110.steps.text" = "Devices, Install, XSide module in the app: Next and Back, clickable steps, and Install only at the last one.";
"whatsNew.110.review.title" = "Review the options each time, or not";
"whatsNew.110.review.text" = "\"Review the options at each install\" is on by default. Off, an app already installed shows the full list of what will apply, with Edit, then Install.";
"whatsNew.110.previews.title" = "Every option explained, with a preview";
"whatsNew.110.previews.text" = "In the install window, each XSide option has a line of explanation and a preview of the bar, the late alert, the card and the notification.";
"whatsNew.110.where.title" = "Where to find it afterwards";
"whatsNew.110.where.text" = "A highlighted box says where to change these settings later, with the app's name: Settings > Apps > YouTube > XSide Settings, or touch and hold the app's icon.";
"whatsNew.110.noFeatures.title" = "Install without XSide features";
"whatsNew.110.noFeatures.text" = "For an app that refuses to launch because it detects a change, install it as it came, per app or for all, after a confirmation that lists what's lost. XSide still refreshes it.";
"whatsNew.110.appWindow.title" = "My apps, in Settings";
"whatsNew.110.appWindow.text" = "Settings > My apps: pick the device, then one of its apps, to set the XSide module in the app on that device, applied live if it is open, otherwise at its next opening or refresh. An app's ... menu in the panel, or the My apps button, leads there directly.";
"whatsNew.110.status.title" = "Where each change stands";
"whatsNew.110.status.text" = "Per device, XSide says plainly where things stand: app open (changes arrive live), changes at the next opening, what is pending (by name), then \"received your settings\". It never claims a setting is active before that.";
"whatsNew.110.panes.title" = "Settings, reorganized";
"whatsNew.110.panes.text" = "Eleven pages: General, Refreshing, Installing, XSide module in the apps (defaults for new installs), My apps, Notifications, Xcode and signing, Updates, Reports & Logs, Build & contribute, About.";
"whatsNew.110.switch.title" = "A new switch";
"whatsNew.110.switch.text" = "XSide's switches now use the brand gradient, and respond to the keyboard (focus ring, Space).";
"whatsNew.110.inject.title" = "\"Injecting the XSide module\"";
"whatsNew.110.inject.text" = "The install step formerly called \"Adding XSide features\" now has this name, and says when it was skipped.";
"whatsNew.106.updated.title" = "Updated, not just refreshed";
"whatsNew.106.updated.text" = "When you install another version of an app over it, the card in the app says \"Updated by XSide\" (or \"Older version installed\") with the old and the new version.";
"whatsNew.106.versions.title" = "Each app's version";
"whatsNew.106.versions.text" = "The panel shows the installed version of each app, device by device (after their next refresh for apps already installed).";
"whatsNew.106.preflight.title" = "Warned before installing";
"whatsNew.106.preflight.text" = "The install window tells you when an app wasn't built for your device's iOS (it may open in compatibility mode), or is older than the version installed.";
"whatsNew.106.silence.title" = "Notifications per device";
"whatsNew.106.silence.text" = "Turn notifications off for a friend's iPhone from the device's … menu: its apps are still refreshed, quietly.";
"whatsNew.106.cli.title" = "xside pause and xside resume";
"whatsNew.106.cli.text" = "Pause refreshes from the Terminal (xside pause 2h, or no duration until resumed); xside status tells you when they're paused.";
"whatsNew.106.updates.title" = "Updates arrive sooner";
"whatsNew.106.updates.text" = "Checks every hour if you want, and also at launch and after each app refresh.";
"whatsNew.106.text.title" = "Readable in large";
"whatsNew.106.text.text" = "The XSide sheet in your apps follows iOS's text size and scrolls when it doesn't fit. \"Last refreshed\" in Settings gives the exact time.";
"whatsNew.105.inApp.title" = "XSide in your apps";
"whatsNew.105.inApp.text" = "After an install, an XSide sheet says until when the app works. After each refresh, a card at the bottom. And an \"Installed with XSide\" section in Settings > Apps.";
"whatsNew.105.reminder.title" = "A reminder on the phone";
"whatsNew.105.reminder.text" = "The day before it expires, the app reminds you itself, with XSide's logo. The XSide sheet first explains why iOS asks for notifications. It works with modded apps too (like some YouTube builds), which iOS blocked until now.";
"whatsNew.105.trust.title" = "Trusting, without searching";
"whatsNew.105.trust.text" = "After an install, XSide opens the app on the device. If it doesn't trust the developer yet, the right Settings page opens by itself: just tap Trust.";
"whatsNew.105.deleted.title" = "Deleted means deleted";
"whatsNew.105.deleted.text" = "An app deleted from the iPhone is no longer reinstalled by the next refresh: XSide notices, removes it from its list and tells you.";
"whatsNew.105.schedule.title" = "Choose when to refresh";
"whatsNew.105.schedule.text" = "1, 2 or 3 days before they expire, a pause (also in the panel), only on power adapter, at night or in the evening. An app about to expire is always refreshed.";
"whatsNew.105.installWindow.title" = "A clearer install window";
"whatsNew.105.installWindow.text" = "A new step, \"Adding XSide features\", shows everything added to the app. In Options, choose for this install whether to open the app and the Trust page. The trust guide gets straight to the point.";
"whatsNew.105.devices.title" = "Devices say what's in the way";
"whatsNew.105.devices.text" = "Tiles show \"Developer Mode off\" or \"Unlock it\". Messages say so too, instead of \"Couldn't create the provisioning profile\", and a device out of reach during an uninstall is reported as such.";
"whatsNew.105.settings.title" = "Lots of new settings";
"whatsNew.105.settings.text" = "Open the app after an install, open the Trust page, notice deleted apps, Wi-Fi for new devices, the reminder on the device and the notification when an app is removed: all in Settings.";
"whatsNew.105.keychain.title" = "Google sign-in fails?";
"whatsNew.105.keychain.text" = "The \"Shared keychain\" option now says when to turn it on: when the app won't sign you in (\"can't sign in\", \"app not verified\").";
"whatsNew.105.report.title" = "Report a problem in one click";
"whatsNew.105.report.text" = "The GitHub form opens already filled in, without naming your apps, and the full log waits on your Desktop. Your personal details are masked. In Settings > Reports & Logs, or with the bug button in the panel.";
"whatsNew.104.updates.title" = "Updates install by themselves";
"whatsNew.104.updates.text" = "Turn on Install updates automatically in Settings > Updates: XSide downloads the new version in the background and installs it as soon as nothing runs, then relaunches.";
"whatsNew.104.cli.title" = "xside in the Terminal";
"whatsNew.104.cli.text" = "xside status, xside refresh youtube, xside install app.ipa… Turn it on in Settings > General. It even starts XSide if it isn't running.";
"whatsNew.104.notify.title" = "Updates you don't miss";
"whatsNew.104.notify.text" = "A new version shows a notification and a banner in the panel, and you're told once it's installed.";
"whatsNew.104.account.title" = "When Xcode drops your account";
"whatsNew.104.account.text" = "Xcode sometimes signs out on its own: one notification, a clear explanation, and refreshes resume once you're back.";
"whatsNew.104.changelog.title" = "Real release notes";
"whatsNew.104.changelog.text" = "The update window shows what changed in the new version, neatly laid out.";
"whatsNew.104.more.text" = "The panel's buttons show their labels on hover again, \"Open Xcode\" tells you how to reach the accounts (⌘ + comma), and a beta Xcode needs its license accepted.";

